{"step_index":1587,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:17:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:17:20-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:17:24-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:17:20-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:17:24-05:00\nShowing lines 1-160 of 442\n1: # Grand Theft Auto VI: Campaign Mission Flow & Prerequisite Guide\n2: \n3: This document provides the definitive mission dependency graph, prerequisite unlock trees, character-switching milestones, heist setup pipelines, points of no return, and speedrun routing across all 5 story chapters of *Grand Theft Auto VI* based on verified data from **Build 1.0.2.1**.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. High-Level Campaign Architecture\n8: \n9: The GTA VI storyline progresses through five distinct geographical and thematic narrative blocks. While open-world exploration is available between operations, missions operate in a strict Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with key narrative bottlenecks connecting each chapter.\n10: \n11: ```mermaid\n12: flowchart TD\n13:     subgraph C1B[\"Prologue & Chapter 1\"]\n14:         C1[\"Just Like Paradise<br/>(Leonida Keys & Key Lento)<br/>Missions 1 - 21\"]\n15:     end\n16: \n17:     subgraph C2B[\"Chapter 2\"]\n18:         C2[\"Paradise Lost<br/>(Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)<br/>Missions 23 - 44\"]\n19:     end\n20: \n21:     subgraph C3B[\"Chapter 3\"]\n22:         C3[\"Vice City Syndicate Expansion<br/>(Vice City Metro & Sinfrontera Heist)<br/>Missions 45 - 70\"]\n23:     end\n24: \n25:     subgraph C4B[\"Chapter 4\"]\n26:         C4[\"Vice City Metro & Airport Takedown<br/>(Ocean Beach & VCIA Cargo Heist)<br/>Missions 71 - 95\"]\n27:     end\n28: \n29:     subgraph C5B[\"Chapter 5\"]\n30:         C5[\"Top of the World, Ma!<br/>(Climax, Standoff & Branching Endings)<br/>Missions 96 - 102\"]\n31:     end\n32: \n33:     C1 -->|\"Bottleneck: Discharge Time [BIL_WHEEL]\"| C2\n34:     C2 -->|\"Bottleneck: Checking Out [BIL_MOTEL]\"| C3\n35:     C3 -->|\"Bottleneck: The Cartel Heist [ROB_BANK]\"| C4\n36:     C4 -->|\"Point of No Return: Sunset [ROB_AIR_END]\"| C5\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 2. Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise (Leonida Keys)\n42: \n43: ### Mechanics & Structure\n44: - **Playable Character**: Strictly locked to **Jason** for early operations, introducing **Lucia** in the Prologue, reuniting in *\"Coming Home\"*, featuring a solo mission for Lucia in *\"Home Sweet Home\"*, and concluding with the joint hospital escape in *\"Discharge Time\"*.\n45: - **Total Missions**: **21 main and side-strand missions** (`replay_menu_position` 0–21 / `story_list_order` 0–22 in `mission_order.json`).\n46: - **Core Narrative**: Petty smuggling, local debt enforcement for Brian, and settling in Key Lento following Lucia's release from Hamlet State Penitentiary, culminating in a violent clash with the Kingfishers, Donnie's death, a botched bag pickup at Grassrivers Visitor Center, the burning of their Hamlet house, and a desperate shootout escape from Vice City Hospital.\n47: - **True 3-Branch Parallel Architecture**: After completing *\"Gone Fishing\"* ($140 mailbox cash pickup), the storyline opens into three concurrent operational tracks:\n48:   1. **Branch 1 (Cal & Brian Marina Jobs)**: *Unwanted Attention* (`COM_KBOS_COLAT` - $200 mailbox cash pickup) $\\rightarrow$ *Pipework* (`COM_KBOS_NEIGHB`). *(Both verified Any% skips auto-flagged by `func_10AA55`)*.\n49:   2. **Branch 2 (Brian Armory & Vehicle Repair)**: *Gear Up* (`FT_AMUCO`) $\\rightarrow$ *Just a Scratch* (`FT_KMODSHP` - Ganado repair & respray; **Mandatory Story Gate**).\n50:   3. **Branch 3 (Rent Collection & Main Spine)**: *Lab Fees* (`COM_KBOS_SHOP` - Any% skip) $\\rightarrow$ *Hey Arnold!* (`COM_KBOS_RADR` - 08:00–16:00 window, Any% skip) $\\rightarrow$ *Feng Shui* (`COM_SFH_MVFN` - triggers mandatory 24h wait) $\\rightarrow$ *Coming Home* (`INT_PRISO` - Lucia released from prison) $\\rightarrow$ *Find Donnie's Package* (`CTI_PIL_RD_SH`).\n51: - **Sub-Branch: Island Dreams (`CSC_TRH_CHART`)**: Unlocked via Kenton's call during *Hey Arnold!*. Optional shipwreck treasure diving side mission (**Any% Skip**).\n52: - **Decision Diamond 1 (Gate Check)**: Evaluates whether the player has completed *Just a Scratch*. If not completed, Joey places an urgent reminder call redirecting Jason back to clear the repair shop gate before *Buck Me* unlocks.\n53: - **Decision Diamond 2 (Smuggler Gate Check)**: Evaluates whether BOTH *Day Release* (`BIL_FUN` - 07:00–17:00 window) AND *Just a Scratch* (`FT_KMODSHP`) are completed before Brian's call triggers *Swamped*.\n54: - **The Chapter 1 Climax Gauntlet (M16–M21)**:\n55:   - **16. Swamped (`INT_AIR`)**: Jason, Brian, and Lori confront the Kingfishers. Donnie is killed, Lori is taken hostage and rescued in the Grassrivers, and Brian retires from smuggling.\n56:   - **Side Branch off Donnie's Death (Any% Skips)**:\n57:     - **17. Don Gone (`COM_KBOS_CLEAN`)**: Brian asks Jason to clean out Donnie's trailer. Exact `0DRP` title is **`Don Gone`**, not \"Doin' Gone\". *(Auto-flagged by `func_10AA55`)*.\n58:     - **18. Recalibration (`HO_PAR_KEYCO`)**: Jason and Lucia take a grieving Cal fishing after Donnie's death. *(Auto-flagged by `func_10AA55`)*.\n59:   - **Main Story Climax Sequence (Mandatory)**:\n60:     - **19. Tourist Trap (`BIL_PICK`)**: Disguised pickup from a locker at Grassrivers Visitor Center. Has day (`BIL_PICK_DAY_TIME_START` 10:00–17:00) and night (`BIL_PICK_NIGHT_TIME_START` 17:00–10:00) triggers. Ambushed by dirty cops; Jason is critically shot! Cal rushes Jason to Vice City Hospital.\n61:     - **20. Home Sweet Home (`BIL_HOUSE`)**: Lucia returns solo to their Hamlet home to retrieve Jason's stash. Ambushed by masked cartel hitmen; Lucia escapes but their home is burned to the ground.\n62:     - **21. Discharge Time (`BIL_WHEEL`)**: **★ TRUE CHAPTER 1 CLIMAX FINALE ★**. Lucia infiltrates Vice City Hospital to save Jason. They fight through dirty cops and cartel gunmen, hijack an ambulance, and flee west across the county line into Port Gellhorn.\n63: - **Transition to Chapter 2 (`MTL_WAKE`)**: Hard cut to Starlet Motel. When `MTL_WAKE` starts, script handler `func_10AA55` sweeps the flag store and automatically marks all uncompleted Chapter 1 side missions as completed.\n64: \n65: ### The 7 Verified Any% Skippable Missions (Auto-Flagged by `func_10AA55`)\n66: In `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs:572964-572999`, when `MTL_WAKE` (0x3C9B93B4) is flagged, the game automatically sets completion flags for all 7 uncompleted side operations:\n67: 1. **Lab Fees** (`COM_KBOS_SHOP`, Hash `0x2D7D2164`)\n68: 2. **Unwanted Attention** (`COM_KBOS_COLAT`, Hash `0x5AE70594`)\n69: 3. **Pipework** (`COM_KBOS_NEIGHB`, Hash `0xC8513199`)\n70: 4. **Hey Arnold!** (`COM_KBOS_RADR`, Hash `0x21D03E4F`)\n71: 5. **Don Gone** (`COM_KBOS_CLEAN`, Hash `0x10BE4C94`)\n72: 6. **Recalibration** (`HO_PAR_KEYCO`, Hash `0x420623AF`)\n73: 7. **Island Dreams** (`CSC_TRH_CHART`, Hash `0x617A1865` — Optional standalone side activity)\n74: \n75: ```mermaid\n76: flowchart TD\n77:     M01[\"1. Prologue<br/><code>INT_PROLO</code> • Lucia Counselor Interview\"] --> M02[\"2. Gone Fishing<br/><code>INT_CHASE</code> • Boat Drop - $140 Mailbox\"]\n78:     \n79:     %% Split Bar into 3 Tracks\n80:     M02 --> B1_Split[\"3-Track Branch Split\"]\n81:     \n82:     subgraph Track1[\"Branch 1: Cal & Marina Odd Jobs (Any% Skip)\"]\n83:         M03[\"3. Unwanted Attention<br/><code>COM_KBOS_COLAT</code> • Cal Hamlet Trip<br/>[$200 Mailbox | ANY% SKIP]\"] --> M04[\"4. Pipework<br/><code>COM_KBOS_NEIGHB</code> • Mandy Maintenance<br/>[ANY% SKIP / AUTO-FLAGGED]\"]\n84:     end\n85:     \n86:     subgraph Track2[\"Branch 2: Brian Armory & Gate (Mandatory)\"]\n87:         M05[\"5. Gear Up<br/><code>FT_AMUCO</code> • Longarm Pickup\"] --> M06[\"6. Just a Scratch<br/><code>FT_KMODSHP</code> • Ganado Respray<br/>★ MANDATORY STORY GATE ★\"]\n88:     end\n89:     \n90:     subgraph Tra