{"step_index":1589,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:17:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:17:20-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:17:24-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:17:20-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:17:24-05:00\nShowing lines 131-260 of 359\n131: PROTAGONIST_TEXT = \"\"\"### Protagonist locks\r\n132: \r\n133: **Observed**\r\n134: \r\n135: - Mission trigger records in `story000.rpf` @ 0x3e2372000 and `levels.rpf` @ 0x11bb116000 carry property\r\n136:   0xDB880157 with one of two values.\r\n137: - Controller lines 635272-635323 read that property. Value 0x4E21D02A is tested against the current player being\r\n138:   `player_lucia` (0xD058819F), value 0x56D7FE7A against `player_jason` (0x072B3FF4). A mismatch sets an output flag.\r\n139: - `ROB_BOAT_L_LUCIA` carries the Lucia value and `ROB_BOAT_J_JASON` the Jason value.\r\n140: - Cross-check: for all 51 entries that have both this property and a recap text, the recap names the same\r\n141:   character. No entry contradicts it.\r\n142: \r\n143: **Inferred.** The property is the character the player must be controlling to start the mission. Entries without\r\n144: the property are `protagonist: null`; that means \"not stated in the data\", not \"either character\".\r\n145: \r\n146: Main-story entries by required player: Jason {jason_count}, Lucia {lucia_count}, differs by variant\r\n147: {both_count}, not stated {none_count}.\r\n148: \"\"\"\r\n149: \r\n150: HOURS_TEXT = \"\"\"### Time-of-day gates\r\n151: \r\n152: **Observed.** Some trigger records carry two integer properties, 0x1FD5BB99 and 0xB376AD2B.\r\n153: `0x947D998BD81F7AC1.ysc.cs` lines 89983-89999 read both into adjacent fields. `story000.ysc.cs` lines 116302-116328\r\n154: enable `BIL_PICK_DAY_TIME_START` when a value is `< 17` and `BIL_PICK_NIGHT_TIME_START` otherwise.\r\n155: \r\n156: **Inferred.** 0x1FD5BB99 is the opening hour and 0xB376AD2B the closing hour. The DAY and NIGHT records of\r\n157: `BIL_PICK` hold mirrored values, which fits. The two data files disagree on some values; which file wins at runtime\r\n158: was not established.\r\n159: \r\n160: {hours_table}\r\n161: \"\"\"\r\n162: \r\n163: OTHER_FILES = \"\"\"### Other files examined for flow data\r\n164: \r\n165: - `story000.rpf` @ 0x35ff74000: a manifest of 609 `.pso.meta` file names (map states, mission areas, `flow`,\r\n166:   `player_schedules_chapter2..5`). It lists names only. The files themselves could not be located by name because\r\n167:   the archive's table of contents is encrypted.\r\n168: - `story000.rpf` @ 0x11b4a0000 (5.5 MB): a hash map of about 67,000 entries, each a key plus two hashes, one of\r\n169:   which is a mission ID for 93 missions. The schema has no ordering or condition field. Purpose not established.\r\n170: - `story000.rpf` @ 0x3e2372000 and `levels.rpf` @ 0x11bb116000: trigger records (position, contact character,\r\n171:   required player, hours, tags). No field references another mission as a condition.\r\n172: - `audio.rpf` @ 0xb92ae0 (71 mission ID hashes): not decoded.\r\n173: \"\"\"\r\n174: \r\n175: NOT_RECOVERED = \"\"\"## Not recovered\r\n176: \r\n177: - Any prerequisite edge (`A` must be done before `B` becomes available). The enabling logic for most missions was\r\n178:   not located. Of 250 calls to the record toggle `_0x480014E54CD33903`, only 9 use a `<CMissions>` ID.\r\n179: - Which missions are strictly mandatory (`is_bottleneck`, `any_percent_required: true`).\r\n180: - The condition that selects `BIL_MOTEL_VIOLENT` versus `BIL_MOTEL_NON_VIOLENT`, and the meaning of the unnamed\r\n181:   argument that selects the `ROB_BOAT` variant.\r\n182: - Names for seven IDs in the story list and most IDs in the side-content list (their titles are known where the\r\n183:   text table has one).\r\n184: - Whether `story000.rpf` or `levels.rpf` trigger data takes precedence where they differ.\r\n185: - Any edge from a finale to `INT_CRED`.\r\n186: \"\"\"\r\n18